      ":question/problem": "${x^{\u2032} = 2x(1 - x) - xy; y^{\u2032} =-2y + 4xy$\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x = x(t)$ represents the prey and $y = y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below. Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium $x^{\u2217} = [1, 0]^{T}$, we get\n\n| $J(x^{\u2217}) =$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $$. |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |"
